<title>USA: Miller Industries names new CFO.</title>
<headline>Miller Industries names new CFO.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Miller Industries Inc said it named Adam Dunayer vice president, treasurer and chief financial officer.</p>
<p>Dunayer was vice president of investment banking at Bear Stearns &amp; Co Inc. and will be responsible for all of Miller's financial operations.</p>
<p>Dunayer replaced Vincent Mish, who was named president of Miller Financial Services Group Inc, the company said.</p>
<p>the largest manufacturer of towing and recovery equipment in the world.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
